.TH MX-SELECT-SOUND 1 "July 2026" "mx-select-sound 26.06.4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mx-select-sound \- select the default audio device
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mx-select-sound
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mx-select-sound
is a graphical utility for selecting and testing the default audio device.
.PP
When PipeWire is running, the program lists available sinks and uses
.BR pactl (1)
to select the default sink.
Otherwise, it lists ALSA sound cards and records the selected default card
in
.IR ~/.asoundrc .
.PP
The
.B Test
button plays a short stereo test sound through the selected default device.
.SH OPTIONS
The program does not provide application-specific command-line options.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.asoundrc
ALSA configuration written when an ALSA sound card is selected.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pactl (1),
.BR speaker-test (1)
